    {
      "v": 9,
      "zh": "不要自己心里说：『有亚伯拉罕为我们的祖宗。』我告诉你们，　神能从这些石头中给亚伯拉罕兴起子孙来。",
      "en": "and don’t think you can say to yourselves, ‘We have Abraham as our father.’[NOTE:1] For I tell you that God can raise up children for Abraham from these stones!",
      "notes": [
        "A winnowing fork was a pitchfork-like tool used to toss threshed grain in the air so that the wind blew away the chaff, leaving the grain to fall to the ground. The note of purging is highlighted by the use of imagery involving sifting though threshed grain for the useful kernels."
      ],
